<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eastern Ganga dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1078–<a href="/years/1434">1434</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eastern Ganga dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Its imperial phase began under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anantavarman-chodaganga">Anantavarman Chodaganga</a>, who conquered the Somavamshi lands around 1110 and began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagannath">Jagannath</a> Temple at Puri. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narasimhadeva-i">Narasimhadeva I</a> built the Sun Temple at Konark. The Gangas were succeeded by the Gajapati kings in 1434.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eastern-ganga-dynasty.jpg" alt="Eastern Ganga dynasty" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amshpatten · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eastern_Ganga_fanam_Chodaganga.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
